# Global orchestration (all repos)

Route work through **modes** in one session: **Explorer → Planner → Implementer → Verifier → (Reviewer)** unless the ask fits a single mode.

## Working agreements

- Investigate and run commands yourself; do not give up after one failure.
- Smallest change that solves the task; no drive-by refactors.
- Read surrounding code before writing; match existing style.
- No git commits, push, or PRs unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not edit markdown/docs the user did not ask to change—unless propagation policy mandates `AGENTS.md` / `skills.md` / `.cursor/rules/` updates.
- Check [PyPI](https://pypi.org/) before adding Python dependencies.
- **Git:** one repo folder, one checked-out branch — no `git worktree add`. Run `git branch --show-current` and `git switch` before any task.
- Long-running Python batch jobs **must** show [`tqdm`](https://pypi.org/project/tqdm/) progress bars — see [`05-tqdm-progress.mdc`](05-tqdm-progress.mdc). Cross-repo workflows: `~/.codex/skills.md`.

## Parallel agent roles

| Role | Activate when | Responsibilities |
|------|---------------|------------------|
| **Explorer** | Unknown area; vague symptom | Trace paths; cite file + line anchors |
| **Planner** | Features, migrations, ambiguous scope | Steps, risks, rollback; Verifier commands from repo `AGENTS.md` |
| **Implementer** | Clear spec or tiny fix | Minimal diffs; match style |
| **Verifier** | After code changes | Run **repo `AGENTS.md → ## Verification`**; paste commands + exit codes |
| **Reviewer** | Pre-PR; sanity check | Risks/regressions; do not rewrite unless asked |
| **Data Analyst** | CSVs/spreadsheets/charts | Transform copies; cite source numbers |
| **Migrator** | Deprecations/upgrades | Checkpointed, reversible steps |
| **Skills Author** | Repeat workflows or corrective feedback | Maintain **`skills.md`** and **`.cursor/skills/`** in sync |

## Classify the ask

| Signal | Start with | Skip |
|--------|------------|------|
| Read-only | **Explorer** | Implementer |
| One obvious line/typo | **Implementer** | Planner |
| Vague symptom | **Explorer** | Planner until entry points known |
| Multi-file change | **Planner** → **Implementer** | — |
| Schema/migration | **Planner** + **Migrator** | Implementer-only refactors |
| User pasted a plan | **Reviewer** pass → **Implementer** | Full Planner unless plan omits verification |
| PR review only | **Reviewer** (+ **Verifier** if CI skipped) | Implementer |

## Standard pipelines

- **Bugfix:** Explorer (if fuzzy) → Implementer → Verifier → Reviewer if PR.
- **Feature:** Explorer (if unfamiliar) → Planner → Implementer → Verifier → Reviewer.
- **Refactor:** Planner (invariants) → Migrator checkpoints → Implementer → Verifier.
- **Build/script/Office deliverable:** Read repo `AGENTS.md` → Implementer → Verifier.
- **Repeatable workflow:** finish with **Skills Author** — update **`skills.md`** and **`.cursor/skills/`**.

## Handoff contract

- **Explorer:** entry files, call path, blocking questions only.
- **Planner:** ordered steps, risks, rollback, definition of done, Verifier commands from repo `AGENTS.md`.
- **Implementer:** changed paths; 1-line intent per file.
- **Verifier:** every applicable command from repo `AGENTS.md → ## Verification`; exact commands + exit codes.
- **Reviewer:** ranked risks; tests skipped and why.

Optional label: `Mode: Verifier` before that phase's output.

## Loops

- **Verifier failed** → Implementer (smallest fix) → Verifier; no new features while fixing.
- **Plan wrong after edits** → Explorer (delta) → amend Planner (*Revised plan*).
- **Reviewer ship-stopper** → Implementer → Verifier → short Reviewer delta.
- **Negative feedback on a `skills.md` / `.cursor/skills/` workflow** → **Skills Author** rewrites matching skill **before** rerun.

Cap: after **two** failed Verifier cycles on the same bug, **Explorer** re-validates assumptions.

## Authority order

1. Repo `AGENTS.md` (closest to cwd wins).
2. Explicit user instructions in the current task.
3. `~/.cursor/rules/` and `~/.codex/AGENTS.md`.
4. Generic best practices.

Safety (secrets, destructive git, production/clinical data) overrides convenience—state once.

## User prefixes

| Prefix | Mode chain |
|--------|------------|
| `Explore only:` | Explorer only — no edits unless blocker |
| `Plan only — no edits:` | Planner — zero file edits |
| `Implement + run tests:` | Implementer → Verifier |
| `Review diff for merge risks:` | Reviewer; rerun Verifier if CI skipped |
| `Data only:` | Data Analyst (+ Implementer if scripts must change) |
| `Migration / upgrade:` | Planner + Migrator checkpoints |
| `No tests — user-approved:` | Skip Verifier; cite waiver once |
| `Skills revise:` | Skills Author — rewrite `skills.md` + `.cursor/skills/` before rerun |

## Anti-patterns

- Implementer skipping Verifier when repo has checks.
- One-shot huge refactors without Migrator checkpoints.
- Mutating authoritative data without explicit approval.
- Long Explorer with no handoff.
- Re-running unchanged skill workflow after user pushback (stale skill — revise first).
